pyenhance: fix common problems in Python source files, in place.
Fixes (select with --select, disable 'is' with --no-is): regex escaped regex
literals ("\\d+") passed to re.* or assigned to *pattern*/*regex* names -> raw
(r"\d+") escape invalid escape sequences ("\d", "\s") -> doubled backslashes
(identical runtime value) bytes non-ASCII characters inside bytes literals
(SyntaxError) -> \xHH escapes is `x is "lit"` / `x is 3` (SyntaxWarning) -> `x
== "lit"` / `x == 3` Every rewrite is validated (compiles, AST unchanged apart
from the intended fixes) before anything touches disk.
Edits are byte-level, so formatting is preserved.
